// expect: 16
// A NESTED FUNCTION'S LATER SIBLING RESOLVES TO A TOP-LEVEL NAMESAKE.
// SYNTAX §«Nested function declarations»: nested fns share a local letrec
// scope, so `first`'s call to `later` is the sibling below it: 5 + 1 + 10.
// The program answers 110: nested fns are bound in sequence, so at `first`
// the name `later` is still the top-level fn that returns 100 (measured
// 2026-09-25; `mentl check` is clean). Without the top-level namesake the
// same program refuses with E_MissingVariable.
//
// Retires when a block's nested fns are one letrec frame whose references
// are edges drawn at the frame's close (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn later(n) = 100

fn outer(k) = {
  fn first(n) = later(n) + k
  fn later(n) = n + 1
  first(5)
}

fn main() = outer(10)
